A||||4||2xsess||Drive alxe replacement and Thanks to Brian the toolmaker||||10||
Z||000000||2xsess||03-04-2001||07:55 PM||||Well, my left CV joint started amking that old scary popping noise today, oddly enough it was right after I mistakenly went through about 1 1/2' of standing water. Silly puddle fooled me. So off to the parts store I headed but first I looked in my manual to see if it listed the size of the nut on the hub end of the axle, nope. So I got online AIM and find Brian a.k.a Sluppy also online so I ask him if he knows. He says no but he'll go take a tire of his car and see what size it is. I say no that's too much to ask and before I can argue anymore he tpes, brb(be right back) well, 5 minutes later he comes back having taken a tire off his car and measuring the nut he tells me that he doesn't have a socket that big but it measures 1.15". <B>I want to Thank Brian again for going out of his way to help me out</B> It endd up being 30mm, file that for future reference <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Needless to say that the job was a pain in the A$$. On top of that there power went out at my house for about 4 hours (think the Army forgot to pay the light bill). I won't repeat the language the came from under the wheel well of my car today but it is all done now and I'm off to go take a test drive.<P>C-Ya<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Wade87GT||03-04-2001||08:10 PM||||Thanks for the info about the 30mm socket and saving me some time. Looks like I'll be starting a clutch job in the AM<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000002||2xsess||03-04-2001||09:37 PM||||OUCH....clutch bad word!<P>I figured someone would benefit from my experience.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Formula88||03-05-2001||12:16 AM||||Don't just get a regular 30mm socket, although one will work.  They make 30mm Axel sockets, that are much deeper, six sided instead of 12 point, and thicker walled.  These are also strong enough for impact gun usage.  You can get them at NAPA, or most parts stores.  It's a standard size for a lot of GM front drive axles, too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ur2biteme||03-05-2001||06:28 AM||||2xsess:<P>guess you missed me on AIM.  i went through the "lets figure out what size this !@#$^@# nut is" for a few days a while back.  oh well<P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>aproaching 173k :)(didnt update for a while)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A>||||reg||1
